  "step_3": "The decision reason relies on identifying which lottery is more left-skewed, defined as assigning greater probability to favorable outcomes. This aligns directly with the individual’s focus on the 'higher winning chance' in Lottery A. Although the term 'skewness' is not used, the cognitive process—comparing the probability of achieving a favorable (non-zero) outcome—matches the core of the decision reason. The individual’s justification (favoring A due to higher chance of winning) corresponds to preferring the more left-skewed lottery. Therefore, the reasoning pattern is consistent with the decision reason, even if not articulated in technical terms.",
